<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:51:17Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Nigeria's upcoming election marred by rising AI disinformation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:229044eb65f29fe020e51c060c2c09d06a6ce00955bf9d10d2d64b446e7d10e6</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:51:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T21:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897--e1618bd315dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Nigeria inches closer to the 2027 polls, the use of artificial intelligence in the electoral process has prompted questions about integrity and institutional readiness. Can Nigerians trust their democratic processes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Sudan pushes back elections amid violent flare-ups</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d3a0eaba929e8f2ed614595ddc68bfa60e6fbf5967767edc30d557c90996942f</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:51:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T20:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-pushes-back-elections-amid-violent-flare-ups/a-79949622--9cf2f881ff78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-pushes-back-elections-amid-violent-flare-ups/a-79949622?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Sudan has been independent from Sudan since 2011, and has not yet held national elections. Since then, the country faces cycles of violence after a civil war led to a tenuous peace deal.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Sudan: Misery worsens amid plummeting aid for displaced people</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd2ef6f3980dfe177bfec257dead69a3e7bf23771879963b394ea5efaf9c7c83</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T08:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sudan-misery-worsens-amid-plummeting-aid-for-displaced-people/a-79938864--624277167dba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sudan-misery-worsens-amid-plummeting-aid-for-displaced-people/a-79938864?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sudan's humanitarian crisis is exacerbated by cuts in international aid. Almost 34 million people are in need as war and drone strikes are making it difficult to deliver aid to the population.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal Youth Olympics in Dakar end on high note</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1fdc9c98e8d841ac9db745611c7fbf9b3636e1f2883efd8f47dfa8a7881fd0c</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T04:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/senegal-youth-olympics-in-dakar-end-on-high-note/a-79944820--d8ec73fdda7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/senegal-youth-olympics-in-dakar-end-on-high-note/a-79944820?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Enthusiastic crowds attended the games in Senegal, with China taking home the most gold medals. It's the first Olympic Games since Russia's war on Ukraine where Russian athletes can compete under their own flag.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20672002626114fba9573e25626b1a4cdc0642454d19ccc5aacedec002b53bcf</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Controversial kinship: From colonial rule to the Holocaust?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a9f3d5e84ef4570563b7e229b4af6215519f7d2b4af2842418eaf4bc2793da0</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228--16129c6452e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hitler once called Eastern Europe "Germany's India." A new exhibition examines the links between colonialism and Nazism, and the bitter debate over where comparisons illuminate history and where they fall short.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
